  "description": "Start here for ci-observe E2E runs. Recent failed tests come first, then captures that are missing their session span, then one row per run. Click a run ID to open its investigation; the same menu links the run comparison dashboard.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 0,
  "links": [],
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Start here",
      "description": "How to read this page: the run ID format, the links, and the time range.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 11,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "tempo",
        "uid": "ci-observe-traces"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Start here\nOne row per E2E run whose test spans arrived, newest first. Click a run id to open it.\n\n**Four words.** A **span** is one timed step inside a test. A **trace** is all the steps of one operation. A **capture** is one CI run with recording on, and its id is the run id in the tables below. A **cohort** is a set of captures that differ only in what you want to compare.\n\n| To answer | Open |\n| --- | --- |\n| Which runs exist, and which failed | this page |\n| What happened inside one run | [**CI Observe — Run Investigation**](/d/ci-observe-runs/ci-observe-e28094-run-investigation) (click a run id) |\n| Where the run's minutes went, step by step | [**CI Observe — Run evidence**](/d/ci-observe-run-evidence/ci-observe-run-evidence) |\n| What the cluster did during a run | [**CI Observe — Cluster**](/d/ci-observe-cluster/ci-observe-cluster) |\n| Did two runs get slower | [**CI Observe — Compare runs**](/d/ci-observe-compare-runs/ci-observe-compare-runs) |\n\n**Reading a run ID**: `vmaas-main-41310072671-a1` means suite `vmaas`, branch `main` (a pull request shows `pr123`), GitHub workflow run `41310072671`, and attempt `a1` (the first attempt).\n\n**Missing session span** means the run's summary span never arrived. The tests may still have passed; the table lists what did arrive. A run that is completely absent never sent any telemetry.\n\n**Time range**: keep the default 7 days. A narrow range can hide a long run. If a run you expect is missing, widen the range up to the 7-day maximum before concluding it never ran."
      },
      "targets": []
    },
